# Line ending and diff policy for C:Type.
#
# NOTE ON TEXT FILES
# ------------------
# A global `* text=auto` rule is deliberately NOT set here. This repository's
# history already stores text files with CRLF in the index, so enabling
# normalisation would rewrite the line endings of every tracked source file the
# next time it is touched. That is worth doing, but it must be a dedicated
# `git add --renormalize .` commit of its own so the churn is reviewable in
# isolation, rather than drip-feeding through unrelated changes.
#
# Until then, line endings in the working tree come from the local
# `core.autocrlf` setting. This repo is developed on Windows with
# `core.autocrlf=true`. See ROADMAP item D5.
#
# The declarations below are safe to add now: they only affect files that Git
# must never EOL-convert or line-merge, and they cause no renormalisation.

# Graphics
*.png binary

# Audio
*.wav binary

# Native and managed binaries
*.so  binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary

# Fonts
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
